      "writtenOn": "2023-03-31T18:33:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately I don\u0027t think we\u0027ll be able to accept this patch.  The main reason being that having more than one codegen unit leads to nondeterministic output from the compiler which is unacceptable for artifacts produced by the buildbots.  This would also impact the performance of several host tools that get run often.\n\nTo address your productivity concerns I have two points:\n\n1) Have you tried setting `SOONG_RUSTC_INCREMENTAL`?  That may get you some of the productivity gains you\u0027re looking for.\n\n2) I\u0027ve revived the discussion about re-purposing engineering builds to be \"quick and dirty.\"  I think that we\u0027d be able to make the changes from this CL or similar changes for that configuration.",
      "revId": "f7f29d1bdbbb5baf52781ec1c051343b62ee1d70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
